      DESCRIBE
STATS -- STATISTICS ON NUMERIC VECTORS.

   MEAN V        THE AVERAGE.
   MEDIAN V      THE MIDDLE VALUE, OR THE MEAN OF THE TWO.
   MODE V        THE MOST FREQUENT VALUE, OR VALUES.
   RANGE V       THE GREATEST LESS THE LEAST.
   VAR V, SD V   SAMPLE VARIANCE AND STANDARD DEVIATION.
   PVAR V, PSD V THE SAME FOR A WHOLE POPULATION.
   P QUANTILE V  THE VALUE A FRACTION P OF THE WAY UP.
   SUMMARY V     LEAST, QUARTILES, MEDIAN, GREATEST, MEAN, SD.
   ZSCORE V      EACH VALUE IN STANDARD DEVIATIONS FROM MEAN.
   RANK V        THE RANK OF EACH VALUE, TIES AVERAGED.
   FREQ V        DISTINCT VALUES AND THEIR COUNTS.
   N HIST V      A HISTOGRAM IN N BINS.

ON TWO VARIABLES, X AND Y OF ONE LENGTH:

   X COV Y       SAMPLE COVARIANCE.
   X CORR Y      CORRELATION.
   X REGRESS Y   LEAST SQUARES: THE INTERCEPT, THEN A SLOPE
                 PER COLUMN OF X, A VECTOR OR A MATRIX.
   X RESID Y     Y LESS THE FITTED LINE.
   X RSQ Y       THE FRACTION OF THE VARIANCE THE FIT EXPLAINS.
   B PREDICT X   THE LINE B AT NEW X.

TESTS, EACH GIVING THE STATISTIC AND ITS DEGREES OF FREEDOM:

   M TTEST1 V    ONE SAMPLE AGAINST A MEAN M.
   X TTEST2 Y    TWO SAMPLES, VARIANCES POOLED.
   CHISQ T       A CONTINGENCY TABLE T, ROWS BY COLUMNS.
   NORMAL Z      THE STANDARD NORMAL DISTRIBUTION AT Z.
   PNORM Z       THE TWO-SIDED PROBABILITY OF A Z THAT LARGE.

RANDOM, FROM THE WORKSPACE'S OWN SEQUENCE:

   RANDU N       N UNIFORM ON 0 TO 1.
   A RANDIN N    N UNIFORM ON A[1] TO A[2].
   RANDN N       N STANDARD NORMAL.
   N SAMPLE V    N OF V WITHOUT REPLACEMENT.
   SHUFFLE V     V IN A RANDOM ORDER.

A MATRIX GIVEN TO A ONE-VARIABLE FUNCTION IS TAKEN AS THE
VECTOR OF ALL ITS ELEMENTS. TYPE HOWQUANTILE, HOWRANK,
HOWHIST, HOWSUMMARY, HOWREGRESS, HOWTEST OR HOWRANDOM.
