      HOWTEST
EACH TEST GIVES TWO NUMBERS: THE STATISTIC, AND THE DEGREES
OF FREEDOM TO READ IT WITH.

M TTEST1 V: T IS THE MEAN OF V LESS M, OVER THE SAMPLE SD
OVER THE ROOT OF N; N-1 DEGREES OF FREEDOM.

X TTEST2 Y: T IS THE DIFFERENCE OF THE MEANS OVER THE POOLED
SD TIMES THE ROOT OF 1÷N1 PLUS 1÷N2, THE POOLED VARIANCE
BEING THE WEIGHTED MEAN OF THE TWO SAMPLE VARIANCES; N1+N2-2
DEGREES OF FREEDOM.

CHISQ T: THE EXPECTED COUNT IN EACH CELL IS ITS ROW TOTAL
TIMES ITS COLUMN TOTAL OVER THE GRAND TOTAL, AND THE
STATISTIC IS THE SUM OF (OBSERVED-EXPECTED)*2 OVER EXPECTED;
(ROWS-1)×(COLUMNS-1) DEGREES OF FREEDOM.

NORMAL Z IS THE PROBABILITY THAT A STANDARD NORMAL VALUE IS
BELOW Z, GOOD TO SEVEN PLACES; PNORM Z IS 2×1-NORMAL |Z, THE
TWO-SIDED PROBABILITY. THERE IS NO T DISTRIBUTION HERE: WITH
THIRTY OR MORE DEGREES OF FREEDOM READ T AGAINST THE NORMAL,
AND WITH FEWER USE A TABLE.
      HOWRANDOM
THE RANDOM FUNCTIONS DRAW ON ROLL, ?, SO THEY FOLLOW THE
WORKSPACE'S RANDOM LINK: FROM A FRESH LOAD THEY GIVE THE
SAME VALUES EVERY TIME, WHICH IS WHAT MAKES A RUN REPEATABLE.

RANDU N IS N VALUES UNIFORM ON 0 TO 1, NEVER EITHER END, AND
A RANDIN N SCALES THEM ONTO A[1] TO A[2]. RANDN N IS N STANDARD
NORMAL VALUES BY THE BOX-MULLER TRANSFORM: THE ROOT OF ¯2
TIMES THE LOG OF ONE UNIFORM, TIMES THE COSINE OF 2 PI TIMES
ANOTHER. N SAMPLE V DEALS N OF V, NO ELEMENT TWICE; SHUFFLE V
DEALS ALL OF THEM.
